## Issue #66 – CD Pipeline Setup Checklist

### GitHub
- [x] Create `staging` environment (Settings → Environments)
- [x] Create `production` environment (Settings → Environments)
- [ ] Optionally add a required reviewer to the `production` environment for manual approval gate
- [x] Add secret: VERCEL_TOKEN
- [x] Add secret: VERCEL_ORG_ID
- [x] Add secret: VERCEL_WEB_PROJECT_ID
- [x] Add secret: VERCEL_SERVER_PROJECT_ID

### Vercel
- [x] Create a Vercel project for the web app (root directory: `apps/web`)
- [x] Create a Vercel project for the server (root directory: `apps/server`)
- [x] Add app env vars to web Vercel project (NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_FORM_URL)
- [x] Add app env vars to server Vercel project (SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, R2_ACCOUNT_ID, R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID, R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, R2_BUCKET_NAME, R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL)
- [x] Set different env var values per Vercel environment (Preview = staging, Production = production) if using separate Supabase/R2 projects per env
- [x] Connect GitHub repo to Vercel projects (Git integration – auto-deploy on push to `develop`)
